  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace to understand the project structure.\nBoth bugs are clear. Let me fix them:\nNow let me verify the existing test runs and passes:\nTest passes. Let me do a quick sanity check on a few extra edge cases:\nCleaned up the scratch file. Let me confirm the preserved files are untouched:\nBoth bugs fixed with one-character-class changes each, no API or test changes.\n\n## Root causes & fixes\n\n**`src/config.ts`** — `enabled()` used `Boolean(value)`, which coerces *any* truthy value (`'false'`, `1`, `[]`, `{}`) into an enabled state. Changed to a strict identity check:\n\n```ts\nexport function enabled(value: unknown) { return value === true }\n```\n\nOnly the literal boolean `true` now enables the feature; `'true'`, `1`, `null`, `undefined`, and objects all resolve to disabled.\n\n**`src/display.ts`** — `display()` had an identical-branch ternary (`value ? 'ON' : 'ON'`), so disabled features still rendered `ON`. Changed the false branch to `'OFF'`:\n\n```ts\nexport function display(value: boolean) { return value ? 'ON' : 'OFF' }\n```\n\n## Verification\n\nThe existing test passes unmodified (`bun test test/oracle.test.ts` → **1 pass, 0 fail, 6 expect() calls**). Signatures are unchanged (`unknown` → `boolean`, `boolean` → `string`), so the API surface is preserved.\n\nI also checked cases the test doesn't cover — `'true'`, `'TRUE'`, `0`, `{}`, `[]` — and every non-`true` input now yields `false`/`OFF`, so the strictness holds beyond just the asserted inputs. Note this is intentional for string config sources: a JSON/`.env` value of `\"true\"` is a *string*, not the literal `true`, and will read as disabled. That matches the requested \"only the literal enabled value true\" semantics, but if string-keyed config files are ever parsed, the coercion belongs at that parse boundary rather than in `enabled()`.\n\nThe scratch file I used for the edge-case sweep was created in the workspace root and removed (`ls -a` confirms only `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, `src`, `test` remain). `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` are byte-identical to their originals, and no configuration was added or test runner substituted."
